            <ArticleTitle>The Role of Invasive Pain Management Modalities in the Treatment of Chronic Pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>103-15</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.mcna.2015.08.011</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0025-7125(15)00149-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Invasive analgesic therapies provide an alternative to medical management of chronic pain. With the increasing incidence of chronic pain not only in the United States but worldwide, more therapies have evolved to address the growing need for pain relief options. These therapies include spinal injections, nerve blocks, radiofrequency ablation, neurostimulation, and intrathecal drug delivery.</AbstractText>
